PROTOTYPE, not applied to any build of this project: the MUL_MAT_ID (MoE) path of ggml-cpu's repack
buffer, with (a) the work handed out dynamically as (expert, column chunk) units instead of a static
row split per thread, and (b) gemm for every group of four or more tokens routed to the same expert
instead of one gemv per token. Behind -DJLLAMA_MMID_V2 (CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS) so one tree builds both
sides of the A/B. Applies to llama.cpp b11887 + llama/patches/ with `git apply`; the measurement
and the correctness check are in docs/benchmarks/moe-mxfp4-cpu-alderlake.md.

